.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH qsh-exec 1  "exec 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-exec \- Run a command on a pinned host and return its output
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh exec\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-env\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIHOST\fR> <\fICOMMAND\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a command on a pinned host and return its output.
.PP
The remote exit code becomes qsh\*(Aqs exit code (255 is clamped to 254); qsh\*(Aqs own failures exit 255. With `\-\-json`, stdout/stderr are returned Base64\-encoded in the envelope; otherwise they are passed through verbatim.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<MILLISECONDS>\fR
Give up with `TIMEOUT` if the command has not finished within this many milliseconds. The remote process is killed
.TP
\fB\-\-env\fR \fI<NAME=VALUE>\fR
Extra environment variable for the remote command (`NAME=VALUE`). Repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fIHOST\fR>
Host alias from the trust store (`qsh trust list`)
.TP
<\fICOMMAND\fR>
The command and its arguments, after `\-\-`
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
